! mcp_bootstrap_p101.strap -- MCP, printed page 101:
! "***** UNIT AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.108, header READ not assumed: the
! top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11011MCP  CARD ID
! BF000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 101".
!
! TWENTY-EIGHT LINES, AND THE COUNT WAS CONFIRMED, NOT ESTIMATED.
! The rightmost column prints the card serial: line 1 is BF000001 and
! line 28 is BF000028, so line N is serial BF0000NN with no break,
! and BF000028 is the last printed row -- the rest of the page is
! blank (the bottom band of the render carries only the form's
! rules).  Nothing fell off the top or the bottom.
!
! >>> THE WHOLE PAGE IS DEFINITIONS, AND IT COMPILES NOT ONE BIT. <<<
! Lines 1-4 are the asterisk box around the heading.  Lines 5-20 and
! 22-28 are TWENTY-THREE SYN cards.  Line 21 carries nothing but a
! comment.  A SYN deposits no storage word, so this deck's entire
! check surface is TWENTY-THREE SYMBOLS AND ZERO LISTING ROWS -- the
! convention printed pp.24, 98 and 99 established.  The BINARY OUTPUT
! column prints "+00000000" and a data description "BU,NN ,10" on all
! twenty-three rows; that is the column working correctly on a
! definitions page and it must NOT be faked into a !CHECK.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS.  Printed p.99 opened the second punched deck of
! this assembly and defined the CHANNEL-UNIT STATUS TABLE; printed
! p.100 is sixteen comment cards and compiles nothing; this page
! defines the UNIT AREA TABLE, the nine-word block whose address the
! status table's SUNAA field (p.99 line 19) points at.  Word 0 holds
! the channel and unit numbers, word 1 the IOD-card count and the
! mount-reminder time, words 2-3 the evaluation table/mask and the
! file-area and control-word addresses, word 4 the last I/O
! instruction, word 5 the MCP return address and control op code,
! word 6 the scratch pad, and words 7-8 the tape-only entries (label
! mode and density, file count, reel addresses and count).
!
! FIRST AND LAST PRINTED LOCATION on the page: line 5 prints
! 000000.14+ and line 28 prints 000010.40+.  These are SYN VALUES,
! not an assembly address -- the location counter does not move on
! this page at all.  THE JOIN TO THE NEIGHBOURING PAGES is therefore
! not a location chain: printed p.99 line 11's SLC,(8)215000. set the
! counter to 215000.00, printed p.100 compiles nothing, and this page
! compiles nothing, so the counter is still 215000.00 when printed
! p.102 begins.  The SLC below records that and nothing else uses it.
! THAT PREDICTION IS NOT TESTABLE AGAINST p.102 and I did not pretend
! otherwise: PDF p.109 prints "PAGE NUMBER 102" over the heading
! "***** FILE AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****" and its rows are SYN
! cards too (line 5 "S ACT AD SYN (BU,19), 0.32" at 000000.40+), so
! its LOCATION column prints SYN VALUES, not an assembly address.
! The join has to be checked against the next page that compiles.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 21, AND WHY IT IS NOT TRANSCRIBED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 21's LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT columns are empty, its NAME
! and STATEMENT columns are empty, and its only content is the
! comment "-ENTRIES FOR TAPE ONLY", which is a heading for lines
! 22-28.  It compiles nothing either way.
!
! >>> AND IT BREAKS THE "DASH IN THE FLAG COLUMN" RULE, WHICH IS THE
! REUSABLE FINDING ON THIS PAGE.  Lines 1, 3 and 4 print a "-" in the
! one-character column between BINARY OUTPUT and NAME (x = 2330..2372
! at 300 dpi).  LINE 2 DOES NOT, AND NEITHER DOES LINE 21 -- checked
! at 1200 dpi, where lines 20's and 22's "S" is the only ink anywhere
! near that x and lines 2 and 21 are blank there.  But line 2 is
! UNAMBIGUOUSLY a comment card: it prints
! "-***** UNIT AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****-" with an empty LOCATION
! and an empty BINARY OUTPUT.  So that column is NOT a per-card
! comment flag on this page.
!
! WHAT EXPLAINS ALL FIVE LINES WITH NO EXCEPTION is the RAW CARD
! IMAGE reading: a comment card is printed verbatim from card column
! 2 on, and column 2 happens to hold a "-" on lines 1, 3 and 4 and a
! blank on lines 2 and 21.  PRINTED p.102 (PDF p.109) SETTLES IT with
! a case this page does not have: its line 10 prints a "-" at that x
! followed by "S REELDSYN(BU,3),2.29" -- a SYN card commented out,
! with the NAME and STATEMENT JAMMED TOGETHER instead of landing in
! their columns, and with an empty LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT.  Its
! line 2 prints "-***** FILE AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****-" with
! nothing at the flag x, exactly as here.  The two reliable tells are
! therefore (a) empty LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT and (b) fields that
! do not line up with the rows above; the dash is just column 2.
! Horizontal position of the comment settles nothing either way,
! because the comment field prints at its literal card column and is
! ragged down the page (line 20's comment starts left of line 22's).
!
! So line 21 is most likely a comment card whose image begins with
! blanks, by the same reading that explains line 2; the alternative
! -- a card with a blank name and statement and only a comment field
! -- is not excluded, and it changes no bit either way.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SPELLINGS ARE SETTLED BY A PRIMARY SOURCE, NOT BY SQUINTING
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! C22-6728-1, "MCP System Analysis Guide", Appendix A "Symbolic I-O
! Control Tables", section "THE UNIT AREA TABLE" (printed p.266,
! figure 147 on printed p.268, the field table on printed pp.269-271;
! PDF page = printed page) tabulates this exact table.  ALL
! TWENTY-THREE NAMES ON THIS PAGE APPEAR THERE, with their bit
! positions.  ALL TWENTY-THREE AGREE ON THE NAME AND ON THE STARTING
! BIT -- which is what the !SYM block below checks -- and
! twenty-two of the twenty-three also agree on the LENGTH.  SSCRPM
! is the exception and is marked (*) below and set out in full
! further down:
!
!   0.12-0.18 SCHANN   0.47-0.49 SUNITN   1.06-1.17 SIODK
!   1.32-1.57 SRMTC    1.62 SUUNAS        1.63 SRMIND
!   2.00-2.18 SEVLTB   2.32-2.50 SEVLMK   3.00-3.17 SFIAAC
!   3.32-3.49 SCWADR   3.60 SRETRY        3.61 SREMNT
!   4.00-4.63 SIOINS   5.00-5.18 SRETAD   5.42-5.49 SCTLOP
!   6.00-6.31 SSCRPM(*)   7.16-7.17 SLABM    7.25 SSYSTM
!   7.29 SLABD         7.38-7.49 SFILEK   8.00-8.17 SFREEL
!   8.32-8.49 SCREEL   8.57-8.63 SREELK
!
! (The Appendix also lists RMCPLB/RPPLB at 6.32-6.63, which this
! page does not define at all.)
!
! That settles the two glyphs this page cannot decide by shape alone:
!   line 13's last character, "S FI AAC" -- round, no left stem, so
!     C or O rather than D, and the comment reads "-FILE AREA
!     ACTIVATED ADDRESS".  Appendix A printed p.269: SFIAAC.  The
!     discriminator was confirmed in the SAME 1200-dpi strip: lines
!     14 and 18 print "ADR" and "AD" with a straight vertical left
!     stem and squared corners, visibly unlike line 13's bowl.
!   line 19's "S CTL OP" and line 17's "S IO INS" -- the round
!     glyphs are O's; Appendix A printed p.270 gives SCTLOP and
!     SIOINS.
! The C/D pair gave no other trouble: line 7's IODK, line 10's
! SRMIND, line 14's ADR, line 18's AD and line 24's LAB D all print
! the D stem, and line 8's RMTC ("-REMINDER MESSAGE TIME CONSTANT"),
! line 28's "S C REEL" ("-CURRENT REEL ADDRESS") and line 13's AAC
! all print the stemless bowl.
!
! >>> (*) ONE PLACE WHERE THE LISTING AND APPENDIX A DISAGREE.  It is
! recorded, not "corrected" -- the listing is the primary artifact
! and C22-6728-1 is a later revision of a different document.
!   LINE 20 IS "S SCR PM SYN(BU,64),6.0", confirmed twice on its own
!   row (the data-description column prints "BU,100 ,10" and 0o100 is
!   64), i.e. the scratch pad is the WHOLE of word 6.  Appendix A
!   printed p.270 gives SSCRPM as bits 6.00-6.31, thirty-two, and
!   puts RMCPLB (if MCP UAT) / RPPLB (if PP UAT) in 6.32-6.63.
!   Neither RMCPLB nor RPPLB is defined anywhere on this page.
!   Transcribed as printed: BU,64.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT ACTUALLY CHECKS WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * NO ROW IS AN INDEPENDENT BINARY CHECK, because there are no rows.
! * NO SYMBOL ON THIS PAGE IS REFERENCED BY ANY LANDED DECK.  A grep
!   of decks/, strap/ and tests/ for all twenty-three names returns
!   nothing, so not one of them is corroborated by another page's
!   transcription and none of them can fail a merge.  Every !SYM
!   below therefore rests on this page's own ink plus Appendix A.
! * EACH SYMBOL IS CHECKED TWICE BY THE PAGE ITSELF, and that is a
!   real check of the digits though not of the card: the STATEMENT
!   column prints the bit offset in DECIMAL and the LOCATION column
!   prints the same offset in OCTAL.  All twenty-three agree --
!   0.12/.14, 0.47/.57, 1.06/.06, 1.32/.40, 1.62/.76, 1.63/.77,
!   2.0/.00, 2.32/.40, 3.0/.00, 3.32/.40, 3.60/.74, 3.61/.75,
!   4.0/.00, 5.0/.00, 5.42/.52, 6.0/.00, 7.16/.20, 7.25/.31,
!   7.29/.35, 7.38/.46, 8.0/.00, 8.57/.71, 8.32/.40.
!   THE DATA-DESCRIPTION COLUMN GIVES A THIRD RENDERING OF THE
!   LENGTH, in octal: BU,07=7, BU,03=3, BU,14=12, BU,32=26, BU,01=1,
!   BU,23=19, BU,22=18, BU,100=64, BU,10=8, BU,02=2.  All agree with
!   the SYN(BU,n) written in the statement.
! * APPENDIX A CORROBORATES ALL TWENTY-THREE SPELLINGS AND BIT
!   POSITIONS, with the one disagreement above.  It is a different
!   document and a later revision; treat it as corroboration of the
!   SPELLINGS -- which listing_oracle can never check -- and not as
!   verification of the transcription.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! CONVENTIONS AND OMISSIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  The NAME column prints "S CHAN N", "S UNIT N", "S IODK",
!     "S RMTC", "SUUNAS", "SRMIND", "S EVL TB", "S EVL MK",
!     "S FI AAC", "S CW ADR", "S RETRY", "S REMNT", "S IO INS",
!     "S RET AD", "S CTL OP", "S SCR PM", "S LAB M", "S SYSTM",
!     "S LAB D", "S FILE K", "SFREEL", "S REEL K", "S C REEL"; only
!     SUUNAS, SRMIND and SFREEL are printed closed up.
! (2) A SYN VALUE WRITTEN "2.0" IS WRITTEN 2.0 VERBATIM; lines 26 and
!     27 print a space after the comma ("SYN(BU,18), 8.0") and that
!     is dropped, SYN not being an entry-mode pseudo-op.
! (3) LINES 1-4 AND 21 COMPILE NOTHING AND ARE NOT TRANSCRIBED: 1, 3
!     and 4 are the asterisk rules, 2 is the heading
!     "-***** UNIT AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS *****-", and 21 is the
!     comment discussed above.
! (4) THE LAST THREE LOCATIONS ARE NOT MONOTONIC AND THAT IS NOT A
!     MISREAD: lines 26, 27 and 28 print 000010.00+, 000010.71+ and
!     000010.40+, because the deck punches SFREEL, SREELK, SCREEL in
!     that order while the field order in word 8 is SFREEL (8.00),
!     SCREEL (8.32), SREELK (8.57).  Appendix A lists them in field
!     order; the cards are in card order.  A SYN does not advance the
!     location counter, so nothing depends on the order.
! (5) NOTHING ELSE.  No printed spelling on this page was refused by
!     strap_asm; there is no substitution anywhere in this deck.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ONE of the twenty-eight line numbers carries an asterisk
! right after it ("5*", "28*"), exactly as printed p.99 does.  That
! is the line-number column and not the mark that sits after a
! LOCATION on pp.3/37/88/97/98.  No location on this page carries a
! mark.  Every location prints a trailing "+" -- the sign, printed as
! a suffix the way printed p.84's negative SYN prints "000001.00-".
! It is dropped in the !SYM lines below because listing_oracle's
! loc_bits parses "word.bit" and has no sign field, which is what
! printed p.99's deck does.

        SLC, (8)215000.0            ! not printed on this page; the
                                     ! counter stands where p.99 line
                                     ! 11 left it.  Nothing here uses it.

! ---- ***** UNIT AREA TABLE DEFINITIONS ***** (lines 1-4) ----------
SCHANN  SYN(BU,7), 0.12             ! line  5 -CHANNEL NUMBER
SUNITN  SYN(BU,3), 0.47             ! line  6 -UNIT NUMBER
SIODK   SYN(BU,12), 1.06            ! line  7 -NUMBER OF IOD CARDS
                                     !           FOR UNIT
SRMTC   SYN(BU,26), 1.32            ! line  8 -REMINDER MESSAGE TIME
                                     !           CONSTANT
SUUNAS  SYN(BU,1), 1.62             ! line  9 -UNIT ALREADY
                                     !           UNASSIGNED IF EQ 1
SRMIND  SYN(BU,1), 1.63             ! line 10 -REMINDER MESSAGE
                                     !           INDICATOR
SEVLTB  SYN(BU,19), 2.0             ! line 11 - EVALUATION TABLE BASE
                                     !           ADDRESS
SEVLMK  SYN(BU,19), 2.32            ! line 12 - EVALUATION MASK
                                     !           ADDRESS
SFIAAC  SYN(BU,18), 3.0             ! line 13 -FILE AREA ACTIVATED
                                     !           ADDRESS
SCWADR  SYN(BU,18), 3.32            ! line 14 -CONTROL WORD ADDRESS
SRETRY  SYN(BU,1), 3.60             ! line 15 -I/O RETRY INDICATOR
SREMNT  SYN(BU,1), 3.61             ! line 16 -AWAITING CORRECT REEL
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0             ! line 17 -IO INSTR. LAST
                                     !           EXECUTED
SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0             ! line 18 -RETURN ADDRESS IN MCP
SCTLOP  SYN(BU,8), 5.42             ! line 19 -OCTAL CONTROL OP CODE
SSCRPM  SYN(BU,64), 6.0             ! line 20 -SCRATCH PAD MEMORY

! ---- -ENTRIES FOR TAPE ONLY (line 21) -----------------------------
SLABM   SYN(BU,2), 7.16             ! line 22 -MODE SPECIFIED IN
                                     !           LABEL
SSYSTM  SYN(BU,1), 7.25             ! line 23 -SYSTEM TAPE FLAG
SLABD   SYN(BU,1), 7.29             ! line 24 -DENSITY SPECIFIED IN
                                     !           LABEL
SFILEK  SYN(BU,12), 7.38            ! line 25 -FILE COUNT
SFREEL  SYN(BU,18), 8.0             ! line 26 -FIRST REEL ADDRESS
SREELK  SYN(BU,7), 8.57             ! line 27 -CURRENT REEL COUNT
SCREEL  SYN(BU,18), 8.32            ! line 28 -CURRENT REEL ADDRESS

